"Into The Wild
Not a great movie, but the book is decent, and the story is more than interesting.
Chris was not your ordinary college graduate.
He took many risks.
He had many ideas and held himself and others to strict moral rules.
His travels, time living in the Alaskan wilderness, and attempt to keep away from his family was far from mature.
He went about things the wrong way.
However, I feel he deserves a lot of credit.
Having dreams that he pursues, when many others wait too long and never get a chance.
I don't think Chris was carefree and footloose as some may think.
I get the feeling he was quite unhappy.
Avoiding and keeping his life a secret from his family takes a lot of energy.
More energy than it takes to just pick up the phone and call them once in awhile.
He is traveling alone and keeping far awy from others, but I think in reality he is trying to gain attention.
Anyway, his story will continue to amaze me and as I grow older I'm sure my views and opinions about his story will also continue to change.
Here's a photo from my hike half way up Mount Rainer"],[[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[]
"じてんしゃ　タイム
In America, especially California, we depend on our cars.
I know some parts of Japan are car culture, but many cities I've been in, train and bikes rule.
I like Kyoto because of this reason.
For the most part, bikes rule.
The trains are fairly pricey and it's a small city in regard to area, thus making じてんしゃ my means of transportation.
It's nice to rely on myself for getting around town.
I feel more connected to the world around me when I ride my bike often.
Trains and cars you can feel very detached from it all, being protected from many elements.
There's no escaping these elements on a bike.
Also, if you see someone you know, it's far easier to stop and say hello.
In a car you see the building rush past you.
It's easy to not pay attention to the things that are important.
On trains you have the option of a book, which is nice, but there's still something missing.
The exercise and connection to the world around is hard to beat."],[[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[]
