"abstract of my graduation thesis 
Analysis of relocating U.
S.
military base in Okinawa and implication for Korea
Young-Eun Kim
Study of international relations, CUK
To maintain the unipolar hegemony, U.
S.
wanted to share the military burden with its allies in North East Asia particularly Japan.
After the 9\/11 terrorist attack in U.
S., more aggressive strategies have been driven in Northeast Asia based on US-Japan alliance and more military roles have been expanded by Japan with U.
S.
global strategy.
The reorganized US-Japan alliance since the Bush administration has been aimed at 3 points below: (1) strategic agreement of shared objectives; (2) embodiment of sharing of military roles; and (3) realignment of  U.
S.
forces in Japan.
In addition, Japanese self-defense force promotes state-of-the-art facilities, flexible and combined forces from army, navy and air force based on U.
S.
transformation strategy as mobile and flexible army.
Therefore the reorganization of US-Japan alliance means ‘military integration’.
The alliance of United States and Japan, during Hatoyama and Obama administrations, is found to have a crack due to different criticisms about the issue of relocating the military base in Futenma, Okinawa.
The conflict of Okinawa military base relocation consists of internal and external causes.
The internal causes are: (1) the configuration of the Hatoyama administration; (2) fails of predictions for the Obama administration; and (3) historical conflict, military base politics and Japan's 21st century grand design.
On the other hand, the external causes are: (1) the geopolitical value of Okinawa; (2) the strategic flexibility of U.
S.
Forces in Japan; (3) the contradictory situation of the U.
S.
military presence in Okinawa (compared to U.
S.
and Japan security contract in 1960); and (4) the reasons for keeping the peace regime of Korean peninsula.
The conflict has great impact on the foreign affairs and national security issue in Japan and even combines with Japanese historical situation and domestic political and social problems.
It will have big ripple effect on Northeast Asian national security.
Relocation of the U.
S.
force in Okinawa will be a good guide to some U.
S.
military bases in Korea since both countries (Japan & Korea) have similar situation.
Therefore, Korean government should work out countermeasures to minimize the national security conflicts in the future."],[[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[]
"mi hermano viene a casa de militar!!
