"FAQ
1) Do you offer private or group classes?
We offer both!
If you want to study with a friend or other people let us know and we will arrange it for you!
Nevertheless we are a specialist in privat online teaching and mostly we offer private classes, because you will have plenty of time to ask questions and practice the foreign language- speaking skills with your tutor.
2) Where are the teachers from?
Our teachers are from all over the world They all have extensive experience teaching their native language as a second language, both in their respective countries and around the world.
3) Where are the students from?
Our students are from all over the world – Europe, Asia, Africa, America and Australia.
4) Who are the typical students at Learn Over IP?
Our students come from all walks of life.
They are business executives, students, housewives, scientists, doctors and immigrants, who want to learn the langauge of the country, in which they will immigrate.
5) Is tutoring for students of every level?
At Learn Over IP we have conversation and pronunciation classes for Beginners, Intermediates and Advanced students.
6) How long are the classes and what are the available times?
Lessons starts every hour, on the hour, and last 50 minutes.
Our classes are available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.
7) What is the curriculum?
The lesson plan focuses on conversation and pronunciation.
Our students have a choice between 3 study programs.
8) What is the difference between an online lesson and classroom instruction?
Online learning offers flexibility in today's fast-paced world.
You can study and learn a language online at your own pace, in the comfort and convenience of your home, office or where ever you want.
9) Do I need a high-speed connection?
Yes it would be preferable to have a high-speed connection.
We recommend to have at least a 100 mb\/s Internet connection..
10) Do I need to download any special computer programs?
Yes you will need to download Skype or Windows Live Messenger.
To download these programs, please visit the following Web site: http:\/\/www.skype.com\/download\/ Skype or: http:\/\/www.microsoft.com\/downloads\/details.aspx?displaylang=en&FamilyID=...
These are software applications that let you talk over the Internet for free.
Skype or MSN are very easy to download.
The sound quality is excellent.
It is as clear as a telephone conversation and in most cases better.
11) What hardware accessories do I need?
A good computer with an acceptable screen.
Don't destroy your eyes while learning a language.
Laptop and TFT screens are good enough now.
You will also need a headset with a built in microphone.
The Web camera is optional
12) What are the methods of payment?
We accept payment with Visa, Master card, American Express and Discover through Paypal or Moneybookers.
Paypal and Moneybookers are secure payment processors that guaranties safety of your online transaction.
They are the two of the preferred and safest online payment methods around the world.
13) What does the price include?
The listed prices include taxes, registration fees, transaction fees and some teaching material.
It is also free to download and talk on Skype or Windows Live Messenger.
* Deutsch
