"Journal Entry #4 : School Cultures
There are many ways that Spanish speaking countries are different from English countries.
One way that Spanish speaking countries are different is that school years are longer.
I think that is good because students have longer period of time learning.
Another difference that we share is the relationship between teachers and students.
In our county we have a informal relationship with teachers we say Mr.
and Mrs then a last name in Spanish they use only \"Profe\".
The teaching is also different because we get to have dicuss
discusssions during class."],[[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[]
