:))"],[[],[],["Ella [sline]está[\/sline] [f-bold][f-blue]es[\/f-blue][\/f-bold] muy loca y simpatica. Well I can't explain you very well the differences between ser or estar, because I just know them, but I can give you a tip. Ser is used with permanent statuses, for example: Mi cabello es de color negro, ese perro es muy bonito, que rápido eres; and Estar is used with no permanent statuses, for example: Estoy cansado (I'm tired, but then I'll recover my energy), estoy sentado junto a mis amigos (I'm sat next to my friends, but I won't be sat always). Obviusly we have some exceptions."],["Ella es marrón y blanc[f-bold]o[\/f-bold], [sline]con un[\/sline] [f-bold][f-blue]y su[\/f-blue][\/f-bold] vientre rosad[f-bold]o[\/f-bold]."],[],["También, [f-bold]a[\/f-bold] Zoey le gusta comer mucho!"],["[f-bold]a[\/f-bold] Ella le gusta comer comida de personas."],["Amo [sline]a Zoey tan mucho![\/sline] [f-bold]muchísimo a Zoey![\/f-bold][sline][\/sline]"],[]
