"Application for a seminar
Every person is different; it should be that but we create (make?) stereotype based on our occupation and nationality.
The stereotype sounds so ridiculous (silly?) but very curious topic for me when I study different culture and international communication.
People create it when they find from a person something weird or different from them.
Every time when I hear those stereotypes, they never match to the person who I know.
For example it is said that Japanese is shy and silent but I’m outgoing and talkative.
There should be serious Mexican or silent Chinese.
However, somehow, every such distorted view always convinced me of the truth in some points, so it makes me wonder and fascinated more and more.
Sometimes I got difficulty to understand the joke in the conversation because of the lack of my knowledge of the stereotype.
I love to talk with my foreign friends, so I’d like to know it and follow their conversation.
Moreover, I want to make them laugh and think  that it is interesting to talk with me.
So I want to study about jokes and English describing about different cultures.
If I study about joke and get the ability to handle it smoothly, it will be so effective for my friendship with my foreign friends and in the business life.
I’m thinking to work in a different country, so the ability of making humour in English should be so necessary thing for my future."],[[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[]
