"Takasebune : 高瀬舟
Miércoles 5 de octubre
De las cien novelas seleccionadas, la cuarta es \"Takasebune\".
\"Takasebune\" es el escrito de \"Ogai Mori\" en 1916.
El tema principal es la entanasia.
\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/
Takasebune era un barco remo en Takasegawa en Kyoto en la era Tokugawa.
En ese momento,los delincuentes arrestados en Kyoto fueron enviados a Osaka por Takasebune.
Un día, \"Shobei\", el hombre remando Takasebune,recogió un criminal poco inusual.
Le llamaba \"Kisuke\".
Fue detenido por matar a su hermano.
Shobei tomó muchas personas a bordo,y todos ellos estaba triste.
Pero,Kisuke parecía ser feliz.
Desde Shobei preguntado, le pidió a Kisuke una razón por la que parecía estar contento.
Kisuke perdió a su padres por la enfermedad, y viviría solo con su hermano 
Aungue eran pobres, vivían de ayudarse unos a otros.
Ellos estaban contentos.
Pero, su hermano se enfermó,tuvo que dejar de trabajar.
Se convertió difícil vivir para ellos,pero Kisuke hizo todo lo que pudo para apoyarle.
Pero, un día, cuando volvió su casa, encontró su hermana se echó con muchas sangres.
Intentó le mató, porque no esperó por causar el problema para Kisuke.
Apuñaló a su cuello con un cuchillo,pero no rogró matarle y guardó el cuchillo en el cuello.
Kisuke intentó llamar a un doctor, pero su hermano le preguntó tirar de el cuchillo.
Dudó hacer sí,pero dibujó el cuchillo porque su hermano le prequntó apacionadamente.
Su hermano murió.
Una mujer vieja vio la escena, lo cuentó funcionario.
Entonces fue detenido, y montó en Takasebune.
Takasebune que se llevo a dos personas silencioso se fueron desvaneciendo en la noche oscura.
\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/ 
Debía de triste.
Pero, al mismo tiempo,se esntía un poco feliz para liberar a su hermano.
¿Qué piensa sobre su acto?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Takasebune : 高瀬舟
One hundred selected novels.
4th \"Takasebune:高瀬舟\"
\"Takasebune\" is the written by \"Ogai Mori\" in 1916.
It's main theme is euthanasia.
\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/
Takasebune was a ship rowing in Takasegawa in Kyoto in Tokugawa era.
At that time,criminals arrested in Kyoto were sent to Osaka by Takasebune.
One day, \"Shobei\" ,the man rowed Takasebune, picked up an unusual criminal.
His name was \"Kisuke\".
He was arrested for killing his brother.
Shobei took a lot of people on board, and all of them was sorrowful.
However, Kisuke seemed to be happy.
Since Shobei wondered, he asked Kisuke a reason why he seemed to be glad.
Kisuke lost his parents by disease, and he lived just with his brother.
Though they were poor, they lived by helping each other.
They were happy.
However,his brother got sick, and he had to stop working.
It became hard for them to make ends meet, but Kisuke did his best to support him.
But, one day,when he went back his home, he found his brother lay down with a lot of blood.
He tried killing himself, because he did not hope to cause trouble for Kisuke.
He stabbed his neck by knife,but he failed to kill himself and keep the knife stabbing in his neck.
Kisuke tried to call a doctor, but his brother asked him to draw the knife.
Kisuke hesitated to do so, but he could not but draw the knife because his brother asked passionately.
His brother died.
An old woman saw the scene, and she told officials that.
Then he was arrested, and he rode on Takasebune.
Takasebune that took two silent people were fading into dark night.
\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/\/
He must be sad.
But, at the same time,he felt a little happy to free his brother.
What do you think about his act?"],[["Takasebune : 高瀬舟"],["Miércoles 5 de octubre"],["De las cien novelas seleccionadas, la cuarta es \"Takasebune\"."],["\"Takasebune\" es el escrito de \"Ogai Mori\" en 1916.
