"journal entry #4 : school cultures
The school length in Spanish-speaking countries is different in the United States.
In the US, usually our school year is 180 days.
In Latin America or Spain, they have 185 to 235 days in school.
They are more focused onacademics.
Here, in the US, we are well-rounded students.
I prefer a shorter school year because i want more time away from school.
I wouldn't beupset if we had to have longer school years because it gives me more time to grow academically.
Schools in Spanish-speaking countries are very different from schools in the United States."],[["journal entry #4 : School Cultures"],["The school length in Spanish-speaking countries is different than it is in the United States."],["In the US, one school year is usually 180 days."],[],["They are more focused on academics."],[],["I prefer a shorter school year because I want more time away from school."],["However, I wouldn't be upset if we had to have longer school years because it gives me more time to grow academically."],["Schools in Spanish-speaking countries are very different than schools in the United States."]
