"La invitación a mi amiga
Hola!
Ati, ¿Cómo estás?
¿Qué haces este fin de semana?
¿Tienes algún plan?
Han abierto un zoológico en mi ciudad.
Voy a visitar allí el sábado que viene con mis padres y tambieén quiero que vengas con nosotros.
Vamos a ver muchos animales que viven en Africa como elefante, cebra, león.
hien y varios aves
Vamos a llevar comida.
Ya sabes que la comida que se vende afuera es cara.
Mi mam dijo que prepararía sandwich con jamón.
Ella cocina muy bien.
Si tienes ganas de ir al zoológico.
llámame para que yo decida la hora a la que nos encontremos."],[[],[],["A tí, ¿Cómo estás? (Hola! a tí, is not used, but it does sound nice)"],["¿Qué harás este fin de semana? (In spanish exist future tenses of verbs, \"harás\" is the future, 2° person, plural tense of \"hacer\")"],[],[],["Voy a visitar lo el sábado que viene con mis padres y quiero  que vengas con nosotros. (\"lo\", in this case, replace things  which were already specified (\"zoológico\" in this case)"],["Vamos a ver muchos animales que viven en Africa como el  elefante, la cebra, el león, (before nouns (almost always) you must use \"el\", \"la\", \"un\" or \"una\", in this post:http:\/\/lang-8.com\/81524\/journals\/262884 I explained when to use each.)"],["hien y varias aves. (I don't know what you mean by \"hien\". \"varias\" must be \"varias\" and not \"varios\" becuase \"aves\" is female, and \"varias\" also. Altought that, it would be more correct to say \"varios tipos de aves\", here \"varios\" is used, because \"tipos\" is male.)"],[],[],["Mi mamá dijo que prepararía sandwiches con jamón. (mam is  not used in normal spanish (maybe some people use it, but  most don't), mamá is like a word used in all languajes, you could also use the real spanish word \"madre\". You must  use \"sandwiches\" because it is plural (unless she will prepair just one sandwich, then you must say: \"Mi madre dijo que prepararía un sandwich con jamón\")"],["[sline]Ella cocina muy bien.[\/sline] This is  not correct, because you don't cook a sandwich. \"cocinar\"  refers to preparing meal with use of heat, it is fully equal to   \"cook\". A correct form may be \"Ella prepara muy rica  comida\" or somethig like that."],["Si tienes ganas de ir al zoológico, (pay attention to the dots and commas, you put a dot, and the proper was a comma)"],[]
"Traducir
Fishermen face new EU penalties if caught
A penalty point system resembling those applied to driving offences is being proposed by Europe’s fisheries chief.
Licensed fishermen who accumulate too many points over three years could face suspensions of six and then 12 months – finally having their permit withdrawn.
The system would apply to the vessel and everyone on board.
The new rules would also govern EU vessels fishing outside European waters, and non-EU vessels in Union waters.
European Fisheries Comissionner Joe Borg:
“Our collective failure to adequately implement and monitor the rules which we agree on undermines the credibility of all our management measures, and it makes a mockery of the system based on catch limitations.”
A country failing to uphold the rules could find its EU subsidies and annual catch quotas cut and even face a ban on fishing in its waters.
Borg also proposed making it compulsory for EU countries to inspect fish landings, processing, transport and sale.
Under the proposed reform, officials from one country could inspect vessels from another.
