"No more excuses not to learn
So now I'm on this website, I really have to learn.
Well, it's a good thing, because I'm a procrastinator at times or a bad perfectionist who wouldn't do anything at all if I know I would fail.
I'm getting down to it though.
I would like to learn Spanish and French...
both of which I have learned and forgotten altogether!
So, let me introduce myself a bit.
I'm Japanese, 27 years old, living in California.
I have been in the US for roughly 2 years.
I have always loved to learn foreign languages and cultures...
They are just so interesting and fun to me!
I used to be a model, but I'm having a hiatus for now....
I don't know if I want to do it again though.
But I know God will open the door for me when the right thing comes up.
I wholeheartedly trust in the Lord that if I follow Him I will find my life.
So as you can see, I'm Christian, and I'm firm on my faith.
But it doesn't mean that I exclude non-believers or people of other religious beliefs.
I don't think religions should hinder friendships.
Well, I will try to write something in either Spanish or French next time I write in here.
Have a wonderful day, people!
:)
Maya"],[[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[]
"Hola a todos!
Hola!
Me llamo Maya, y soy de Japon.
He estado viviendo en California desde el verano 2008.
Digo el japones y el ingles con soltura.
Amo bailar y me gustaria aprender el flamenco un dia.
Tambien, me gusta leer y tengo muchos libros.
No me gusta la ciencia ficcion, pero ademas de que, lei algo.
Me gusta la musica tambien.
Escucho a R&B, jazz, roca, musica pop, clasica etc.
Tengo una gata y su nombre es Moko, no Moco.
Moko significa suave o mullido en el japonés cuando es repetido dos veces como moko-moko.
Es muy bonita.
Quiro majorar mi espanol.
Ayudame por favor!
Muchas gracias antemano :)
Hasta luego!
