no estoy traduciendolo correctamente.
La primera casa por donde pasábamos era tan hermosa que parecía un palacio.
The first house that we passed was so beautiful it looked like a palace.
Sus dueños eran los ricos del pueblo, y  no tenían hijos.
The owners were the richest people in town and they didn't have children.
Estos últimos les debía causar mucha pena, porque eran muy aficianados a los niños
Being without children made them very sad because they loved children very much.
Su mejor gusto, siempre que íbamos a la escuela o volvíamos a casa para almorzar, era asomarse al balcón que daba sobre el camino.
(This sentence really frustrates me)
To his\/her great pleasure, when we were on our way to school or returning home for lunch, he\/she would always appear on the balcony that faced the road.
(How do you know which one would appear on the balcony?
Is it the husband or the wife???)
De allí hablaban con nosotros y nos echaban regalitos.
They would talk to us from the balcony and throw us little gifts.
Gracias"],[["Entiendo las palabras [f-red]individuales[\/f-red] pero...."],[],["La primera casa que pasamos era tan hermosa que parecia un palacio"],[],["Los dueños eran la gente mas rica del pueblo y no tenian hijos"],["The owners were the rich[sline]est[\/sline] people in town and they didn't have children. [f-blue](los ricos=the rich people, the rich ones; the richest=los más ricos)[\/f-blue]"],["no tener hijos los ponia muy triste porque ellos amaban mucho a los niños."],["Being without children made them very sad because they [sline]loved[\/sline] [f-blue]were very fond of[\/f-blue] children [sline]very much[\/sline]."],["para su mayor gusto, cuando ibamos camino a la escuela o regresando a casa para almorzar. el\/ella siempre aparecia en el balcon que daba a la calle."],["(This sentence really frustrates me) [f-blue](As translation exercise: forget \"su mejor gusto\". Then try to translate the text between the commas, finally the text after the comma. Realize that the sentence talks about the childless couple... hint su=their) :-)[\/f-blue]"],["To his\/her great pleasure, when we were on our way to school or returning home for lunch, he\/she would always appear on the balcony that faced the road. (you are on the right track... here's my version: [f-blue]What they liked best, each time that we went to school or returned home for lunch, was to look out from the balcony that faced the road[\/f-blue][f-blue].)[\/f-blue]"],["(How do you know which one would appear on the balcony? [f-blue](They are talking about the childless couple. What they liked to do was... to look out from the balcony... they=the couple)[\/f-blue]"],["Is it the husband or the wife???) [f-blue](I think that \"su mejor gusto\" talks about the couple, so the couple appeared on the balcony - su=their)[\/f-blue]"],["desde el balcon hablarian con nosotros y nos lanzarian pequeños obsequios(regalos) "],["They would talk to us from the balcony [f-blue](from there)[\/f-blue]and throw us little gifts."]