"Japanese-American takes chess tourney over the best in the world.
I often wonder why there aren't more professional chess players from Japan.
Many other Asian countries have very strong players.
The current world champion is from India and China has many Grand Master's of chess but Japan has very few GM's.
Why?
I know Japanese people are some of the smartest people on the planet.
I guess it just isn't popular there.
Anyway, this is the man I spoke of in the title:  http:\/\/www.chessgames.com\/perl\/chessplayer?pid=10084
This is the tournament he won which included the current world champ and many other top players:  http:\/\/www.chessgames.com\/perl\/chess.pl?tid=72726&crosstable=1"],[[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[]
