"Journal Entry #4 : School Cultures
In Spanish Speaking countries, the classes are lecture - focused classes with no student discussions.
In the United States, the classes are mostly a combination of lectures,student discussion, and hands on activities.
I think the United States is a better place to receive an education because the classes are more interactive with the students and the teachers.
It may also be a disadvantage because the students would be more distracted with all the activities going on."],[[],[],[],[],[]
"Unit 5 EQ
I think that going to school in a Spanish - speaking country  would be similar and different from my school experience in the United States.
It would be similar because I would still have the schooling experience.
I would be difficult and different because I would have the basic understanding of the language, when i do but its not as productive as theirs.
