"journal entry # 4: school cultures
One contrasting element of Spanish speaking vs.
United States schools is the length of the school year.
I would rather prefer the length of the Spanish speaking countries, which are longer.
Why would I prefer a longer school year?
In the United States it may seem as though the school year is already long, but I think it should be longer.
If it is longer students retain more information; however, the summer breaks are shorter.
If the school year were longer, more students would graduate and understand more of the courses in school.
Maybe it's not the length of the school year, it could just be the students.
Having a longer school year in the United States would or could enhance the students' knowledge.
Even though it may shorten the length  of the summer break, most students don't have anything to do.
Most  make the choice to do stupid things that could effect their whole life.
So, I would much rather prefer a longer school length because undergraduates could get a lot out of it!"],[[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[]
