"What's your wish? （願い事はなぁに？）
Today is  TANABATA festival in Japan.
Hoy es el festa de TANABATA en Japón.
Do you know TANABATA?
¿Sabes ......?(+_+)
We celebrate the star Festival on 7th July in Japan.
Celebramos la estrella Festividad es el siete de julio en Japón.
People celebrate the day by writing some wishes on the paper strips which called TANZAKU.
Celebramos eso hoy ...
escribe tu deceos en los papeles......???(+_+)
TANZAKU with colorful decorations are hanged on branches of bamboo set up in the garden.
TANZAKU de colores ...
cuélgalos en los bambúes.
These families who have bamboo decoration on TANABATA are gradually thinned out.
Estas familias ...?(+_+)
However you can see them at some public spaces.
Pero puedes encontrar esos en la publica plaza.
I'm going to prepare for the TANABATA festivel.
Voy a preparar para el festivel TANABATA.
I will eat \"SOMEN\" like vermicellifine noodles.
Voy a comer \"SOMEN\" como fideos vermicellifine.
SOMEN is often compared to a MILKY WAY that is a stage of TANABATA legend on the day.
(^_^)
?(+_+)
My wish is only one!
I want to upgrate my English and Spanish!
Mi deseo es sólo uno!
Quiero upgrate mi Inglés y Español!
