"I made an American friend.
When I went to Japan, I made a friend named Larkin from U.
S.
A.
He has the blue eyes and the dark blond hair.
When I first saw him, he was in the same bus with me and I knew he is a professor of my university.
On third day in Japan, I felt uncomfortable with my seat.
I discovered that the cusion of the seat fell in.
Oh my God!
I thought I have to be on a diet :P Anyway I was looking for another seat but the bus was full of the students.
Then, I flash across my mind the foreiner was seated alone.(There are two seats at one side and I had my partner.) Initially, I hesitated to talk with him because he only speak English.
But I screwed up my courage and I started a conversation.
I told him word by word very clearly 
\" Excuse me.
Could you change the seat with me?
Because the cusion of my seat is so bad\"
He answered immediately.
\" Sure, I can \"
Taking this opportunity,I gradually had the talk with him.
He told me that Koreans are too shy in speaking English.
So I'm unusual and unique person for him.
And he'd like to be the friends with me.
I was happy to hear that.
I also thought we could be the good friends."],[[],[],[],[],["He has blue eyes and dark blond hair."],["When I first saw him, he was in the same bus as me and I knew he was a professor of my university."],["On the third day in Japan, I felt uncomfortable with my seat."],["I discovered that the [f-blue]cushion[\/f-blue] of the seat fell in."],[],["I thought I have to be on a diet :P Anyway I was looking for another seat but the bus was full with the students.
